I told you, we're not using our eyes.

567
00:38:01,751 --> 00:38:06,150
We marked you earlier on, so now we can
track you just by scent.

568
00:38:11,810 --> 00:38:13,010
Summoning jutsu!

569
00:38:14,270 --> 00:38:15,270
Rashomon!

570
00:38:22,810 --> 00:38:23,810
Impressive.

571
00:38:24,210 --> 00:38:27,450
Rashomon is our greatest defense for Lord
Orochimaru.

572
00:38:27,650 --> 00:38:31,650
And for him to dent it like
that... But it doesn't matter.

573
00:38:36,150 --> 00:38:38,050
This is the end!

574
00:38:47,290 --> 00:38:48,010
Akamaru!

575
00:38:48,011 --> 00:38:49,011
No!

576
00:38:49,070 --> 00:38:51,030
You were trying to protect me!

577
00:38:52,230 --> 00:38:54,110
He did it again!

578
00:38:55,350 --> 00:38:56,490
My eyes!

579
00:38:57,214 --> 00:38:58,330
Damn it!

580
00:38:58,650 --> 00:39:00,710
This is worse than the last time!

581
00:39:00,850 --> 00:39:02,890
It's... some sort of acid!

582
00:39:03,170 --> 00:39:05,550
My eyeballs feel like they're burning!

583
00:39:06,350 --> 00:39:07,350
Where'd the other one go?

584
00:39:08,130 --> 00:39:09,130
Boo.

585
00:39:11,170 --> 00:39:12,850
Looking for someone, kid?

586
00:39:15,280 --> 00:39:17,150
Go wash your eyes in that river.

587
00:39:17,330 --> 00:39:18,870
I'll take care of the rest.

588
00:39:23,110 --> 00:39:23,670
Use it, 가난 파근.

589
00:39:23,671 --> 00:39:25,190
A unique ability I know.

590
00:39:25,710 --> 00:39:26,870
Helps with assassination.

591
00:39:27,710 --> 00:39:31,990
A sharp sense of smell and a set of claws
aren't gonna be enough to beat me.

592
00:39:33,010 --> 00:39:35,630
Face it, you're in over your head,
little dog.

593
00:39:37,890 --> 00:39:41,373
You know that the network in
our bodies through which chakra

594
00:39:41,374 --> 00:39:44,670
passes is deeply interwoven
with our organs, do you not?

595
00:39:45,370 --> 00:39:48,158
Do you know that the network
in our bodies through which

596
00:39:48,159 --> 00:39:48,850
chakra passes is deeply interwoven
with our organs, do you not?

597
00:39:48,851 --> 00:39:50,046
The cells that make up our organs.

598
00:39:50,070 --> 00:39:52,490
The cells that make up those tissues.

599
00:39:53,510 --> 00:39:59,710
Even within each individual protein,
the very building blocks of our cells.

600
00:40:01,030 --> 00:40:05,252
Once in stage two, I'm able
to use chakra to dismantle

601
00:40:05,253 --> 00:40:08,670
and reconstruct these
cells and proteins at will.

602
00:40:09,030 --> 00:40:14,150
Breaking my body down into tiny particles,
I seep into my opponent.

603
00:40:14,151 --> 00:40:18,010
Then return to my original form inside
their body.

604
00:40:18,590 --> 00:40:19,590
Akamaru!

605
00:40:19,930 --> 00:40:22,550
I'm... sorry, Akamaru.

606
00:40:23,770 --> 00:40:27,370
But... I think this time we're sunk,
old friend.

607
00:40:28,330 --> 00:40:31,950
My cells are swimming freely throughout
your body.

608
00:40:32,250 --> 00:40:35,090
I can even generate parts that are solely
yours.

609
00:40:35,510 --> 00:40:38,850
In other words, we're slowly fusing
together.

610
00:40:39,190 --> 00:40:41,170
We'll be sharing a body.

611
00:40:42,530 --> 00:40:43,530
Sharing?

612
00:40:44,150 --> 00:40:44,570
A body?

613
00:40:45,070 --> 00:40:46,070
That's right.

614
00:40:46,470 --> 00:40:49,650
I'm going to snuff out your life as only I
can.

615
00:40:49,910 --> 00:40:54,250
By eradicating all the cells in your body
from the inside out.

616
00:40:54,830 --> 00:40:55,830
I see.

617
00:41:03,640 --> 00:41:05,680
In that case...

618
00:41:13,940 --> 00:41:15,740
What if I do this?

619
00:41:16,300 --> 00:41:17,640
Then what happens?

620
00:41:20,680 --> 00:41:21,680
Suicide?

621
00:41:22,120 --> 00:41:23,220
You're crazy!

622
00:41:26,040 --> 00:41:27,240
Time for you to die.

623
00:41:35,860 --> 00:41:37,420
Are you mad?

624
00:41:37,900 --> 00:41:39,200
What are you doing?

625
00:41:40,540 --> 00:41:42,160
It hurts, doesn't it?

626
00:41:43,020 --> 00:41:43,840
Well, come on.

627
00:41:43,980 --> 00:41:46,060
I know one way to stop the pain.

628
00:41:52,260 --> 00:41:53,260
Sure.

629
00:41:59,980 --> 00:42:03,060
You're just an alligator who's רק за
That's not enough blood for a Fatal Blue.

630
00:42:07,300 --> 00:42:10,720
Who cares anymore if we're less than
family?

631
00:42:14,580 --> 00:42:15,580
Amateallu...

632
00:42:17,780 --> 00:42:18,580
That's not enough blood for a Fatal Blue.

633
00:42:18,581 --> 00:42:21,061
I happen to think I can be a better
valiant of our family here.

634
00:42:23,060 --> 00:42:24,300
Where is he?

635
00:42:25,634 --> 00:42:27,300
The little brat?

636
00:42:38,660 --> 00:42:43,890
So, he ran away and left his little doggy
behind.

637
00:42:44,350 --> 00:42:49,090
A logical decision, but pretty
cold-blooded even for me.

638
00:42:53,980 --> 00:42:54,660
What?

639
00:42:54,661 --> 00:42:56,160
No, it can't be!

640
00:43:10,640 --> 00:43:11,640
It's okay.

641
00:43:11,760 --> 00:43:12,940
He's still breathing.

642
00:43:18,490 --> 00:43:19,490
What a relief.

643
00:43:26,770 --> 00:43:27,780
Good boy, Akamaru.

644
00:43:28,770 --> 00:43:29,960
You really gave it your all.

645
00:43:30,890 --> 00:43:33,320
Thanks to you, we were able to stall the
enemy.

646
00:43:33,620 --> 00:43:35,260
We beat him up pretty good, too.

647
00:43:38,000 --> 00:43:39,000
You rest now.

648
00:43:39,900 --> 00:43:40,900
You've done enough, boy.

649
00:43:58,550 --> 00:44:00,190
I'll kill you!

650
00:44:03,440 --> 00:44:04,440
Hey!

651
00:44:04,940 --> 00:44:05,940
Sakon!

652
00:44:06,200 --> 00:44:07,420
Where are you?

653
00:44:13,100 --> 00:44:13,740
Sakon!

654
00:44:13,741 --> 00:44:14,741
Sakon!

655
00:44:18,015 --> 00:44:19,340
Yeah, yeah.

656
00:44:19,420 --> 00:44:19,940
I hear you.

657
00:44:19,941 --> 00:44:20,941
Stop shouting.

658
00:44:21,295 --> 00:44:23,560
My head's already beating like a gong.

659
00:44:23,880 --> 00:44:24,880
Huh?

660
00:44:25,740 --> 00:44:26,740
Brother!

661
00:44:26,834 --> 00:44:30,800
Right now, all I want to do is find that
brat and tear him to pieces.

662
00:44:31,810 --> 00:44:35,160
But that will have to wait, because now
it's time for me to rest.

663
00:44:35,740 --> 00:44:38,440
If you find him or that mutt, keep them
alive.

664
00:44:39,440 --> 00:44:40,740
I'll kill them when I wake up.

665
00:44:41,140 --> 00:44:41,620
Understood?

666
00:44:41,840 --> 00:44:43,360
You've got a deal, brother.

667
00:44:44,720 --> 00:44:45,720
Only...

668
00:44:46,160 --> 00:44:48,220
We'll do the killing part together.

669
00:44:49,940 --> 00:44:50,940
Yeah!

670
00:45:02,800 --> 00:45:05,100
Now behold... the Will-O-Dance!

671
00:45:30,460 --> 00:45:31,460
Huh?

672
00:45:37,960 --> 00:45:39,540
...What is going on?

673
00:45:41,200 --> 00:45:42,340
Hey, you!

674
00:45:48,590 --> 00:45:49,270
What's going on here?

675
00:45:49,271 --> 00:45:49,650
You're not in any sort of state!

676
00:45:49,651 --> 00:45:50,750
Well, it was you and me!

677
00:45:51,110 --> 00:45:52,110
Really?

678
00:46:10,070 --> 00:46:11,610
What the heck is he?

679
00:46:12,230 --> 00:46:14,690
Bones sticking out of him like a
porcupine!

680
00:46:52,410 --> 00:46:53,990
How does he do that?

681
00:47:00,090 --> 00:47:01,450
Won't be long now.

682
00:47:05,510 --> 00:47:08,650
He's gonna use his own bone as a sword?

683
00:47:17,650 --> 00:47:18,430
It's no use.

684
00:47:18,431 --> 00:47:21,430
This is no ordinary bone.

685
00:47:22,210 --> 00:47:26,470
It's of the highest density, as hard as
tempered steel.

686
00:47:26,890 --> 00:47:27,670
So what?

687
00:47:27,830 --> 00:47:31,170
I'm still gonna break every bone in or out
of your body!

688
00:47:31,630 --> 00:47:34,470
You think you know the limits of my
powers, do you?

689
00:47:37,010 --> 00:47:39,690
I have five dances in my repertoire.

690
00:47:40,550 --> 00:47:41,670
You've only seen one.

691
00:47:42,030 --> 00:47:43,030
Yeah, whatever!

692
00:47:45,970 --> 00:47:48,030
All right, if that's what you want.

693
00:47:48,110 --> 00:47:49,110
I'll let you have it.

694
00:47:49,430 --> 00:47:51,810
Next I'll show you the Camellia Dance.

695
00:47:54,510 --> 00:47:55,510
Come...

696
00:47:55,630 --> 00:47:56,890
What are you waiting for?

697
00:47:56,970 --> 00:47:57,970
Bring it on!

698
00:48:04,430 --> 00:48:07,050
I can smell them... coming this way.

699
00:48:10,120 --> 00:48:11,120
They're close...

700
00:48:17,910 --> 00:48:20,170
I left a trail of blood leading right to
me.

701
00:48:20,870 --> 00:48:24,187
Well, Akamaru, that trick
bought us some time, but it

702
00:48:24,188 --> 00:48:27,170
looks like I may have gotten
a little carried away with it.

703
00:48:41,200 --> 00:48:43,480
That scent... wait a minute.

704
00:48:44,400 --> 00:48:45,400
Why?

705
00:48:45,540 --> 00:48:47,600
What the hell would they be doing here?

706
00:48:48,720 --> 00:48:51,680
I don't know what's going on, but one
thing's for sure.

707
00:48:51,780 --> 00:48:53,000
We gotta beat it.

708
00:48:53,060 --> 00:48:54,060
Fast.

709
00:48:59,460 --> 00:49:00,460
No way.

710
00:49:01,060 --> 00:49:02,260
I'm too dizzy.

711
00:49:02,700 --> 00:49:03,980
Lost too much blood.

712
00:49:04,620 --> 00:49:06,760
Afraid I'm in no better shape than you
are, boy.

713
00:49:11,900 --> 00:49:13,020
Sorry, Akamaru.

714
00:49:43,910 --> 00:49:46,910
So he's traveling by water now,
huh?

715
00:49:46,911 --> 00:49:48,790
What a clever boy.

716
00:49:54,170 --> 00:49:55,330
What a drag.

717
00:50:05,570 --> 00:50:06,570
It's over.

718
00:50:07,630 --> 00:50:09,650
There's nowhere to run this time.

719
00:50:09,890 --> 00:50:11,730
You're trapped like a rat.

720
00:50:14,850 --> 00:50:16,810
Gotta admit, that wasn't bad.

721
00:50:17,550 --> 00:50:18,590
Timing was perfect.

722
00:50:18,950 --> 00:50:21,310
You got all three of them right where you
wanted them.

723
00:50:21,870 --> 00:50:23,510
That's quite a tricky tune.

724
00:50:25,150 --> 00:50:27,590
Something like that must take a lot of
practice.

725
00:50:28,270 --> 00:50:29,650
It does, actually.

726
00:50:30,610 --> 00:50:34,470
So you figured out I was manipulating them
with my flute.

727
00:50:35,110 --> 00:50:36,770
You're not as dumb as you look.

728
00:50:37,330 --> 00:50:39,090
Not that it'll do you any good.

729
00:50:41,170 --> 00:50:41,670
No.

730
00:50:41,671 --> 00:50:44,810
Knowing what I've been doing isn't the
same as knowing how to stop me.

731
00:50:45,690 --> 00:50:47,110
You've got a point there.

732
00:50:47,630 --> 00:50:49,270
I never was very musical.

733
00:50:49,530 --> 00:50:51,090
Just asked my mom and dad.

734
00:50:52,410 --> 00:50:55,630
With that flute, she can manipulate her
buddies like puppets.

735
00:50:55,990 --> 00:50:59,425
That song's comprised of
sequences of modulated sound

736
00:50:59,426 --> 00:51:02,290
waves, each sequence
controlling a specific movement.

737
00:51:04,350 --> 00:51:05,390
Great, Shikamaru.

738
00:51:05,610 --> 00:51:10,070
You can analyze it fine, but what are you
going to do to counteract it?

739
00:51:13,810 --> 00:51:14,810
She's right.

740
00:51:15,410 --> 00:51:18,110
The fact remains that I have no ear for
music.

741
00:51:19,760 --> 00:51:21,810
No one's ever heard this song and lived.

742
00:51:23,195 --> 00:51:24,990
Here's the finale, 9th passage.

743
00:51:25,350 --> 00:51:26,050
Demon pizza.

744
00:51:26,051 --> 00:51:27,051
Revolution.

745
00:51:40,830 --> 00:51:42,270
She changed the tune.

746
00:51:45,210 --> 00:51:46,230
Here they come!

747
00:52:00,550 --> 00:52:01,750
What's happening?

748
00:52:16,330 --> 00:52:17,550
What's he doing?

749
00:52:27,950 --> 00:52:29,210
Wait for it!

750
00:52:36,550 --> 00:52:41,110
The instant he realizes my material ghosts
are about to attack, he evades them.

751
00:52:41,270 --> 00:52:42,790
He's smarter than I thought.

752
00:52:44,670 --> 00:52:45,670
But...

753
00:52:54,750 --> 00:52:58,090
I had to use almost all my paper and smoke
bombs back there.

754
00:52:58,091 --> 00:53:00,850
And all I managed to do was hide...

755
00:53:01,590 --> 00:53:02,830
that white thing.

756
00:53:04,490 --> 00:53:06,710
It took a bite of my physical energy.

757
00:53:13,470 --> 00:53:15,670
That shuriken passed right through him.

758
00:53:15,790 --> 00:53:18,830
These things are more like apparitions
with very little mass.

759
00:53:19,470 --> 00:53:22,190
They're chakra itself, but with an
appetite.

760
00:53:23,610 --> 00:53:27,890
Probably some kind of chakra that draws
its form from eating mental energy.

761
00:53:28,870 --> 00:53:30,510
That's why they crave physical energy.

762
00:53:30,710 --> 00:53:31,910
It keeps them stable.

763
00:53:33,010 --> 00:53:35,221
If I scuffle with those
hungry chakra much

764
00:53:35,222 --> 00:53:38,931
longer, I won't be able
to build up my own chakra.

765
00:53:39,250 --> 00:53:40,630
They're pretty dangerous.

766
00:53:41,850 --> 00:53:45,250
A ninja who can create special chakra like
me?

767
00:53:45,490 --> 00:53:48,270
She must be using some obscure ninjutsu.

768
00:53:49,010 --> 00:53:52,069
Which means I should
leave those ghost things

769
00:53:52,070 --> 00:53:54,890
alone and concentrate on
the one controlling them.

770
00:53:54,891 --> 00:53:58,410
The quickest way would be to go and stop
the sound of her flute.

771
00:54:00,110 --> 00:54:03,410
But with those things around, it would be
impossible to get close enough.

772
00:54:04,510 --> 00:54:05,510
Okay then.

773
00:54:05,730 --> 00:54:10,591
The next best option would be to capture
those three with my shadow possession jutsu.

774
00:54:11,550 --> 00:54:15,550
But that's not gonna happen, since they
never attack me at the same moment.

775
00:54:16,530 --> 00:54:20,630
If I let even one escape, he'd get to me,
and that would be it.

776
00:54:20,890 --> 00:54:21,890
Game over.

777
00:54:22,390 --> 00:54:25,710
She hasn't left me any openings on either
offense or defense.

778
00:54:27,510 --> 00:54:28,510
Heh.

779
00:54:28,550 --> 00:54:30,910
She must be a pretty good shogi player.

780
00:54:33,700 --> 00:54:34,700
Let's see.

781
00:54:34,770 --> 00:54:39,040
My remaining ninja tools are
twelve kunai knives, nine shuriken,

782
00:54:39,041 --> 00:54:43,190
thirty-six feet of wire, one flash
bomb, and one paper bomb.

783
00:54:43,530 --> 00:54:43,970
Heh.

784
00:54:44,470 --> 00:54:45,470
Oh man.

785
00:54:45,570 --> 00:54:48,930
It's like playing shogi without any
bishops or rooks.

786
00:54:53,570 --> 00:54:55,010
There's no use hiding.

787
00:54:56,610 --> 00:54:58,776
Unless you can predict
these guys' movements,

788
00:54:58,856 --> 00:55:00,930
there's nowhere
you can run, little rat.

789
00:55:01,270 --> 00:55:04,250
And when I find you, I'll break you in
two.

790
00:55:06,190 --> 00:55:06,950
Everything's ready.

791
00:55:07,090 --> 00:55:09,430
The only thing left is to get it over
with.

792
00:55:11,450 --> 00:55:12,850
I've got nine moves.

793
00:55:13,310 --> 00:55:14,890
I've gotta win by then.

794
00:55:15,890 --> 00:55:16,890
That's one.

795
00:55:19,610 --> 00:55:20,610
Hm?

796
00:55:26,430 --> 00:55:27,430
Oh, please.

797
00:55:27,750 --> 00:55:30,130
My sound jutsu can't be stopped that
easily.

798
00:55:30,410 --> 00:55:33,570
Whatever you've got planned to beat me,
it's not gonna work.

799
00:55:43,000 --> 00:55:44,000
Two.

800
00:55:44,620 --> 00:55:45,260
Hm?

801
00:55:45,480 --> 00:55:48,120
Now he's scampering around like a little
rat.

802
00:55:48,740 --> 00:55:49,840
Where is he?

803
00:55:54,770 --> 00:55:55,770
Three.

804
00:55:56,850 --> 00:55:57,850
Ah!

805
00:55:58,270 --> 00:55:58,570
Ah!

806
00:55:58,710 --> 00:55:58,910
Ah!

807
00:55:59,070 --> 00:55:59,710
Ah!

808
00:55:59,711 --> 00:56:00,711
Ah!

809
00:57:33,630 --> 00:57:34,710
It can't be.

810
00:57:35,430 --> 00:57:40,250
He could tell their moves by... He's
saying he memorized my finger positions?

811
00:57:41,790 --> 00:57:42,730
There's no way!

812
00:57:42,810 --> 00:57:43,810
That's impossible!

813
00:57:43,850 --> 00:57:46,650
You extend your right index finger and
ring finger.

814
00:57:47,870 --> 00:57:51,470
Then you place the middle finger and pinky
on your left hand the same way.

815
00:57:51,950 --> 00:57:55,290
That sound seems to make the crab man
stand at the ready.

816
00:57:57,210 --> 00:58:01,510
When you press with your right thumb and
index finger, and move your left index

817
00:58:01,511 --> 00:58:05,070
finger and pinky, that causes the big guy
with the club to charge.

818
00:58:06,950 --> 00:58:11,050
While you were wasting all your time
dodging my knife attacks and trying to

819
00:58:11,051 --> 00:58:14,330
locate me, I was observing
each and every one of your

820
00:58:14,331 --> 00:58:17,450
finger moves, and studying
how these thugs reacted to them.

821
00:58:18,490 --> 00:58:20,190
Analyzed and memorized.

822
00:58:28,540 --> 00:58:29,600
Don't even try.

823
00:58:30,360 --> 00:58:32,740
They're bound by my shadow possession
jutsu.

824
00:58:35,640 --> 00:58:38,720
There's one rule of shogi that I always
enjoyed the most.

825
00:58:39,360 --> 00:58:41,760
Whenever you capture
one of your enemy's pieces,

826
00:58:41,761 --> 00:58:44,721
you can turn around
and use it as your own.

827
00:58:45,540 --> 00:58:47,920
From here on, I attack.

828
00:58:48,640 --> 00:58:51,200
I'll use your own three pieces to hunt you
down.

829
00:58:51,340 --> 00:58:52,900
What do you have to say about that?

830
00:58:55,100 --> 00:58:56,960
Shouldn't you be a bit more worried?

831
00:58:57,100 --> 00:58:58,940
You could at least pull a knife or
something.

832
00:58:59,620 --> 00:59:01,120
This flute is my only weapon.

833
00:59:02,520 --> 00:59:03,260
I told you.

834
00:59:03,261 --> 00:59:06,460
Not one person who's heard the sound of
this flute has survived, idiot.

835
00:59:07,050 --> 00:59:08,320
You've got a lot of confidence.

836
00:59:13,720 --> 00:59:14,720
Dispel!

837
00:59:20,000 --> 00:59:24,140
What was all that about using my own
pieces against me, loser?

838
00:59:28,970 --> 00:59:30,700
It's my move now, you rat!

839
00:59:34,750 --> 00:59:35,750
What the...

840
00:59:36,960 --> 00:59:38,460
Shadow possession success!

841
00:59:48,770 --> 00:59:50,050
What did I tell you?

842
00:59:50,410 --> 00:59:52,490
I'd hunt you down using your own pieces.

843
00:59:53,290 --> 00:59:54,650
I used them all right.

844
00:59:54,830 --> 00:59:57,450
Your three pawns were just the bait I
needed.

845
00:59:57,690 --> 01:00:01,070
In any good strategy, the first attack's
always a fake out.

846
01:00:01,690 --> 01:00:04,550
The tactic is to score on the second move.

847
01:00:04,930 --> 01:00:05,930
You bastard!

848
01:00:07,350 --> 01:00:08,350
Yep.

849
01:00:13,790 --> 01:00:14,990
There's no other way.

850
01:00:15,350 --> 01:00:18,130
Now that it's come to this, I'll need to
summon more power.

851
01:00:18,630 --> 01:00:22,110
I didn't think I'd need to go to second
state with a chump like him.

852
01:00:22,470 --> 01:00:23,730
It ticks me off.

853
01:00:24,190 --> 01:00:28,310
But I've got to admit, for a little punk,
this guy was pretty impressive.

854
01:00:35,690 --> 01:00:43,110
...You might have thought you
were pretty sharp as a fighter...

855
01:00:43,111 --> 01:00:46,610
...but from here on, things won't go
according to your plan!

856
01:00:47,190 --> 01:00:48,190
What is she?

857
01:00:48,530 --> 01:00:49,530
...

858
01:00:51,010 --> 01:00:52,010
No way!

859
01:00:52,290 --> 01:00:56,330
Is she strong enough to force herself out
of the Shadow Possession jutsu?

860
01:00:56,331 --> 01:00:58,890
What's up with this tremendous chakra?

861
01:01:00,490 --> 01:01:02,250
My jutsu is gonna fall apart.

862
01:01:02,510 --> 01:01:04,330
I can't worry about conserving chakra.

863
01:01:06,270 --> 01:01:08,330
I have to use my other jutsu.

864
01:01:10,370 --> 01:01:13,050
Ninja Art, Shadow Strangle Jutsu!

865
01:01:20,190 --> 01:01:23,030
Is it choking my body with that shadow?

866
01:01:23,310 --> 01:01:26,250
It feels just like I'm being grabbed by a
real hand.

867
01:01:27,090 --> 01:01:29,270
I am not letting you beat me!

868
01:01:29,890 --> 01:01:30,630
Darn it!

869
01:01:30,750 --> 01:01:32,490
She's got incredible strength!

870
01:01:32,730 --> 01:01:34,830
At this distance, I can't hold onto her!

871
01:01:35,910 --> 01:01:36,990
Take this!

872
01:01:37,770 --> 01:01:40,290
Demon Flute, Chains of Fantasia!

873
01:01:46,990 --> 01:01:48,270
This is bad.

874
01:01:49,130 --> 01:01:51,310
Is this... a genjutsu?

875
01:01:58,030 --> 01:01:59,530
What's he trying to do?

876
01:02:08,290 --> 01:02:08,930
This is bad.

877
01:02:08,930 --> 01:02:08,930
I can't hold onto her!

878
01:02:08,931 --> 01:02:10,930
My body... I can't move!

879
01:02:37,340 --> 01:02:42,120
When I'm at second state, my flute can
unleash all kinds of genjutsu.

880
01:02:42,140 --> 01:02:45,920
Of all of them, this one's particularly
appropriate for that rat.

881
01:02:45,921 --> 01:02:47,520
That's because...

882
01:02:51,155 --> 01:02:55,100
This genjutsu paralyzes its prey and traps
it like vermin.

883
01:02:58,765 --> 01:03:01,700
Tell me, how's it feel to be the one tied
up?

884
01:03:08,180 --> 01:03:09,260
Die, little rat!

885
01:03:13,320 --> 01:03:15,701
How did you... What?

886
01:03:20,430 --> 01:03:22,670
He broke his own finger with this shadow?

887
01:03:22,910 --> 01:03:25,610
The pain it caused must have broken the
genjutsu!

888
01:03:25,970 --> 01:03:29,350
This whole time, he kept pretending to be
trapped by the jutsu!

889
01:03:33,230 --> 01:03:35,270
I already told you this.

890
01:03:35,510 --> 01:03:37,750
The first attack's always a fake.

891
01:03:38,050 --> 01:03:41,390
Its basic strategy, the second move,
wins the match.

892
01:03:41,890 --> 01:03:46,130
You might have noticed my second move was
a little different from before.

893
01:03:46,131 --> 01:03:50,730
With the shadow-strangled jutsu,
the closer I am to my opponent,

894
01:03:50,950 --> 01:03:53,050
the stronger my hold on him will be.

895
01:03:54,590 --> 01:03:55,590
Darn it!

896
01:03:55,950 --> 01:03:58,230
I got careless and came too close!

897
01:03:58,630 --> 01:04:00,390
No, that's not what did it.

898
01:04:02,790 --> 01:04:04,770
Shouldn't you be a bit more worried?

899
01:04:04,890 --> 01:04:06,730
You could at least pull a knife or
something.

900
01:04:07,090 --> 01:04:08,930
This flute is my only weapon.

901
01:04:09,870 --> 01:04:14,990
I told you, not one person who's heard the
sound of this flute has survived, idiot!

902
01:04:15,390 --> 01:04:16,850
So that's why...

903
01:04:17,430 --> 01:04:17,910
Exactly.

904
01:04:18,410 --> 01:04:23,491
The reason I threw my last kunai knife
right in front of you, I missed on purpose.

905
01:04:24,050 --> 01:04:27,106
You said you didn't have any
other weapons, so I knew all

906
01:04:27,107 --> 01:04:29,650
along that you would pick
it up and come closer to me.

907
01:04:33,070 --> 01:04:34,230
I'll give you credit.

908
01:04:34,990 --> 01:04:36,830
You're a lot smarter than I thought.

909
01:04:37,130 --> 01:04:38,910
And a lot more persistent.

910
01:04:40,670 --> 01:04:43,230
On top of that, I'm a nice guy.

911
01:04:43,650 --> 01:04:45,291
Well, my name is...
Most of the time.

912
01:04:45,550 --> 01:04:47,730
You'll have to excuse my bad manners.

913
01:04:47,790 --> 01:04:50,230
I'm not normally in the habit of slugging
a lady.

914
01:04:50,830 --> 01:04:54,830
But then, looking at you, you don't really
fall into that category, do you?

915
01:04:56,110 --> 01:04:57,710
So I guess it's okay.

916
01:05:01,750 --> 01:05:05,450
You may have escaped my genjutsu,
but don't let it go to your head!

917
01:05:05,770 --> 01:05:07,190
You're still a worm!

918
01:05:08,150 --> 01:05:11,210
She's not completely immobilized by my
shadow possession.

919
01:05:12,310 --> 01:05:14,670
Ugh... I've got to
make this count!

920
01:05:20,570 --> 01:05:23,110
Just a little more...

921
01:05:34,030 --> 01:05:35,030
Ugh...

922
01:05:42,810 --> 01:05:44,970
Even at this range...

923
01:05:44,971 --> 01:05:47,627
With her bound up as
tight as I can make it,

924
01:05:47,628 --> 01:05:50,130
she's still got enough
chakra to push back.

925
01:05:50,650 --> 01:05:52,530
Got to keep the pressure on.

926
01:05:52,810 --> 01:05:55,350
Let up for a second and I'll get hammered!

927
01:05:56,550 --> 01:05:57,270
That's it.

928
01:05:57,370 --> 01:06:00,790
If this jutsu doesn't finish it once and
for all...

929
01:06:03,710 --> 01:06:04,710
Ugh...

930
01:06:06,910 --> 01:06:07,910
Ugh...

931
01:06:26,930 --> 01:06:29,490
Ugh... Ugh... Ugh... Ugh...

932
01:06:30,350 --> 01:06:33,211
Ugh... Well, I've got to go, or
I'm really going to be in trouble!

933
01:06:40,650 --> 01:06:43,350
Ugh... Ugh... Ugh!

934
01:06:43,570 --> 01:06:43,650
Ugh...!

935
01:06:43,651 --> 01:06:44,730
Ugh...!

936
01:06:44,731 --> 01:06:45,290
Ugh...!

937
01:06:45,291 --> 01:06:46,770
Ugh...!

938
01:06:46,771 --> 01:06:47,771
Ugh...!

939
01:06:50,910 --> 01:06:51,910
Ugh...!

940
01:07:11,370 --> 01:07:19,370
A little pause... and we are back.

941
01:07:20,270 --> 01:07:22,970
This guy... he's incredible!

942
01:07:24,630 --> 01:07:28,410
All those shadow clones, and not one of
them got through!

943
01:07:29,730 --> 01:07:31,690
It's come at last.

944
01:07:32,670 --> 01:07:34,650
The moment I've been waiting for.

945
01:07:37,350 --> 01:07:42,590
The first step toward achieving Lord
Orochimaru's design.

946
01:07:57,250 --> 01:07:58,250
Sasuke!

947
01:08:01,770 --> 01:08:02,770
Hey, Sasuke!

948
01:08:03,170 --> 01:08:05,010
What are you hanging out with these losers
for?

949
01:08:05,200 --> 01:08:06,200
Come on!

950
01:08:06,330 --> 01:08:07,330
Let's go home now!

951
01:08:13,220 --> 01:08:14,220
Talk to me!

952
01:08:15,100 --> 01:08:16,100
What?

953
01:08:16,470 --> 01:08:17,750
Have you gone deaf or something?

954
01:08:20,820 --> 01:08:21,600
Hey, wait!

955
01:08:21,760 --> 01:08:22,200
Sasuke!

956
01:08:22,620 --> 01:08:23,620
It's no use.

957
01:08:23,720 --> 01:08:24,779
Now die!

958
01:08:27,120 --> 01:08:27,800
Sasuke!

959
01:08:27,801 --> 01:08:28,801
Sasuke!

960
01:08:30,479 --> 01:08:31,479
Sasuke!

961
01:08:33,560 --> 01:08:34,560
Who's this?

962
01:08:38,319 --> 01:08:39,479
In his eye!

963
01:08:40,040 --> 01:08:43,300
The rejuvenated Leaf Village's handsome
devil!

964
01:08:51,010 --> 01:08:52,029
Rock Lee!

965
01:08:59,609 --> 01:09:00,609
Uchi pro!

966
01:09:05,170 --> 01:09:07,310
But what about your injuries?

967
01:09:07,609 --> 01:09:09,090
Do not worry about me, Naruto!

968
01:09:09,350 --> 01:09:10,550
Go get Sasuke!

969
01:09:11,010 --> 01:09:12,010
Really?

970
01:09:12,810 --> 01:09:13,810
Are you sure?

971
01:09:14,550 --> 01:09:15,910
Go on, get going!

972
01:09:16,090 --> 01:09:17,970
I can take care of things here.

973
01:09:21,529 --> 01:09:23,050
This one's strong.

974
01:09:24,470 --> 01:09:25,470
Good.

975
01:09:26,029 --> 01:09:28,149
Okay, but just be careful, will ya?

976
01:09:28,290 --> 01:09:30,850
He uses his own bones for weapons!

977
01:09:31,310 --> 01:09:32,310
His bones?

978
01:09:33,090 --> 01:09:34,090
Interesting.

979
01:09:36,870 --> 01:09:38,029
Watch yourself.

980
01:09:38,590 --> 01:09:41,050
This guy's strength is beyond belief!

981
01:09:41,051 --> 01:09:42,051
Finally!

982
01:09:43,510 --> 01:09:45,189
Then what're you waiting for?

983
01:09:45,390 --> 01:09:46,390
Go!

984
01:09:47,510 --> 01:09:48,689
Thumbs up, Naruto!

985
01:09:48,990 --> 01:09:49,270
Remember?

986
01:09:49,569 --> 01:09:50,710
You gave it to Sakura!

987
01:09:50,970 --> 01:09:52,290
You made her a promise!

988
01:09:55,690 --> 01:09:58,210
I'm gonna bring Sasuke back home no matter
what!

989
01:09:58,650 --> 01:10:00,790
And that's a promise of a lifetime!

990
01:10:02,210 --> 01:10:03,210
Do not worry.

991
01:10:03,250 --> 01:10:04,950
I can finish this one!

992
01:10:06,790 --> 01:10:07,790
I promise!

993
01:10:15,370 --> 01:10:16,390
I don't think so.

994
01:10:18,890 --> 01:10:19,890
You die!

995
01:10:21,870 --> 01:10:23,750
I dislike being ignored.

996
01:10:29,445 --> 01:10:30,950
Good luck, Bushy-brow!

997
01:10:36,220 --> 01:10:40,520
Still, no matter how you look at it,
with Sasuke bottled up in that coffin,

998
01:10:41,505 --> 01:10:44,560
there's not a team of genin on Earth that
can take on that bunch and win.

999
01:10:46,240 --> 01:10:47,240
I'm well aware of that.

1000
01:10:47,960 --> 01:10:48,960
I'm not a fool.

1001
01:10:50,880 --> 01:10:53,940
And that's why I've already taken certain
measures.

1002
01:10:56,380 --> 01:10:57,380
Huh?

1003
01:10:58,195 --> 01:10:59,300
She's in here!

1004
01:11:04,680 --> 01:11:09,900
Guy, what is it?

1005
01:11:09,940 --> 01:11:11,700
Did something happen on your mission?

1006
01:11:12,520 --> 01:11:13,520
No.

1007
01:11:14,560 --> 01:11:15,100
I ran without a hitch.

1008
01:11:15,220 --> 01:11:18,440
And then I ran back as swiftly as my feet
could carry me.

1009
01:11:19,040 --> 01:11:22,480
Who cares about my mission?

1010
01:11:23,380 --> 01:11:26,100
Tell me, how did this surgery go?

1011
01:11:26,340 --> 01:11:27,340
I gotta know!

1012
01:11:32,840 --> 01:11:34,760
It was successful.

1013
01:11:36,200 --> 01:11:39,440
In fact, I've okayed him to start training
tomorrow.

1014
01:11:39,860 --> 01:11:41,360
Going easy at first.

1015
01:11:45,860 --> 01:11:49,360
Well, he probably should stay in bed,
but you know him.

1016
01:11:49,940 --> 01:11:52,020
I'm afraid we have a problem, my lady.

1017
01:11:52,480 --> 01:11:53,540
It's Rock Lee!

1018
01:11:53,760 --> 01:11:55,580
He's disappeared from his room!

1019
01:12:02,680 --> 01:12:06,920
He must have slipped out last night while
I was treating Genma and Raido.

1020
01:12:07,790 --> 01:12:08,790
Little fool.

1021
01:12:09,150 --> 01:12:10,460
He must have gone after them.

1022
01:12:12,420 --> 01:12:13,980
He must have been half delirious.

1023
01:12:14,330 --> 01:12:18,300
Instead of his prescription, he took a
bottle of elixir that I'd left in here.

1024
01:12:34,100 --> 01:12:35,690
Bottle of... elixir?

1025
01:12:38,040 --> 01:12:40,470
Oh, no... Oh, no!

1026
01:12:45,770 --> 01:12:53,770
He is too fast!

1027
01:12:56,290 --> 01:12:58,130
I cannot land a single kick!

1028
01:12:59,690 --> 01:13:03,630
Your agility is impressive, and you have a
most singular style.

1029
01:13:05,450 --> 01:13:07,250
Your style's too direct.

1030
01:13:08,110 --> 01:13:09,410
Almost obvious.

1031
01:13:16,670 --> 01:13:17,670
It's over.

1032
01:13:19,110 --> 01:13:20,290
One moment, please!

1033
01:13:24,690 --> 01:13:28,110
I am so sorry, but I have to take my
medicine at a certain time.

1034
01:13:28,111 --> 01:13:30,350
And that time happens to be now!

1035
01:13:31,160 --> 01:13:32,680
Excuse me, it will take just a minute.

1036
01:13:41,510 --> 01:13:44,530
To be honest, I never really liked
medicine.

1037
01:13:49,910 --> 01:13:54,610
I first noticed this phenomenon on the
night I took Lee to a restaurant to

1038
01:13:54,611 --> 01:13:56,810
celebrate his perfecting the reverse
lotus.

1039
01:13:58,190 --> 01:14:00,410
Thinking it was water, he drank some
water.

1040
01:14:00,411 --> 01:14:01,411
He drank some of my sake.

1041
01:14:04,320 --> 01:14:07,450
A teeny-weeny little cup, barely a sip...

1042
01:14:10,465 --> 01:14:13,830
That's when things turned really ugly.

1043
01:14:14,190 --> 01:14:15,670
What do you mean exactly?

1044
01:14:17,130 --> 01:14:18,970
First, there was this ominous silence.

1045
01:14:20,970 --> 01:14:25,590
A moment later, the entire restaurant was
a disaster.

1046
01:14:26,390 --> 01:14:29,630
As if... as if a tsunami had hit it.

1047
01:14:32,030 --> 01:14:36,410
And then... Whatever it is, it is the
worst tasting medicine I have ever...

1048
01:14:46,710 --> 01:14:47,710
Strange.

1049
01:14:49,190 --> 01:14:51,470
What sort of medicine is it?

1050
01:14:54,750 --> 01:14:56,330
It was pure destruction.

1051
01:14:56,630 --> 01:14:58,990
The likes of which I've never seen!

1052
01:15:02,830 --> 01:15:04,110
And the older, the better.

1053
01:15:04,111 --> 01:15:05,510
What are you staring at?

1054
01:15:05,511 --> 01:15:06,730
You stupid jerk!

1055
01:15:07,310 --> 01:15:10,050
I-I-I-I-I...

1056
01:15:11,190 --> 01:15:14,010
Don't-Don't move, bronzy!

1057
01:15:14,250 --> 01:15:18,710
I-I-I... I knew then
what Lee was.

1058
01:15:19,190 --> 01:15:22,590
A natural-born master.

1059
01:15:26,025 --> 01:15:29,690
A master of the DRAGON FIST!

1060
01:15:30,410 --> 01:15:35,651
If you will not make the first move, then
I will just have to bring the fight to you!

1061
01:15:37,990 --> 01:15:40,710
His style of attack is fairly direct.

1062
01:15:51,100 --> 01:15:52,630
What would you do that for?

1063
01:16:05,650 --> 01:16:11,430
I am enjoying the springtime of my youth!

1064
01:16:14,910 --> 01:16:17,210
His moves are so unorthodox.

1065
01:16:17,570 --> 01:16:19,510
But more than anything, he's fast!

1066
01:16:20,770 --> 01:16:25,090
I am in the prime of my youth and taking
the most of it!

1067
01:16:33,650 --> 01:16:34,830
This is very hard to idiot.

1068
01:16:34,831 --> 01:16:35,090
I will make you pay for the last time!

1069
01:16:35,170 --> 01:16:39,410
I will have you pay for this time and I
will make you pay for this time again!

1070
01:16:40,510 --> 01:16:41,730
I will be watching you for the next time!

1071
01:16:41,731 --> 01:16:42,731
And that's it!

1072
01:16:43,910 --> 01:16:51,910
I will get you, trainer!

1073
01:17:15,030 --> 01:17:16,950
I can't read his movements.

1074
01:17:17,630 --> 01:17:19,630
For him to land an attack on me?

1075
01:17:20,370 --> 01:17:21,890
That's quite the Taijutsu.

1076
01:17:24,330 --> 01:17:26,070
No other choice.

1077
01:17:35,530 --> 01:17:38,770
My true abilities lie within my bones.

1078
01:17:39,310 --> 01:17:42,970
I'm sure the little clone brat must have
told you before he left.

1079
01:17:43,310 --> 01:17:47,630
I think it's time we sobered you up.

1080
01:17:48,090 --> 01:17:49,390
Sober who up?

1081
01:17:49,550 --> 01:17:51,170
Do I look drunk to you?

1082
01:17:53,530 --> 01:17:56,350
Well, whatever you are, I'll snap you out
of it.

1083
01:17:58,230 --> 01:18:00,330
I said I'm not drunk!

1084
01:18:00,970 --> 01:18:03,850
In the first place, I'm not even of age!

1085
01:18:04,630 --> 01:18:07,910
The underage ninja should not partake in
drinking sake!

1086
01:18:18,910 --> 01:18:20,410
Unorthodox, is it not?

1087
01:18:20,411 --> 01:18:23,370
This is my kekkei genkai.

1088
01:18:35,730 --> 01:18:40,130
He wasn't able to scamper off too far with
that wound of his.

1089
01:18:49,800 --> 01:18:50,800
That's it.

1090
01:18:51,240 --> 01:18:52,280
I can't go any further.

1091
01:18:54,180 --> 01:19:02,180
Are you kidding me?

1092
01:19:02,791 --> 01:19:04,210
He's already caught up?

1093
01:19:05,710 --> 01:19:06,710
Then wait.

1094
01:19:07,950 --> 01:19:10,430
My head is pounding like a drum.

1095
01:19:10,670 --> 01:19:12,930
And why is my face bleeding?

1096
01:19:13,970 --> 01:19:17,070
It seems I really was drunk after all
then.

1097
01:19:18,530 --> 01:19:20,670
What has happened to you?

1098
01:19:21,430 --> 01:19:23,850
So, your medicine has finally worn off.

1099
01:19:24,590 --> 01:19:27,070
You're looking at my kekkei genkai.

1100
01:19:28,630 --> 01:19:30,310
Kekkei genkai?

1101
01:19:30,890 --> 01:19:38,250
My kekkei genkai freely controls my
osteoblasts and osteoclasts.

1102
01:19:38,251 --> 01:19:43,870
It allows me to alter the concentration of
calcium and form new bones altogether.

1103
01:19:44,630 --> 01:19:49,210
Normally, the human body contains 206
bones.

1104
01:19:49,430 --> 01:19:53,650
But in my case, that number is somewhat
more negotiable.

1105
01:19:58,690 --> 01:20:02,690
Are those really human bones?

1106
01:20:04,910 --> 01:20:07,070
Very well!

1107
01:20:08,890 --> 01:20:11,310
Behold, my large dance.

1108
01:20:12,530 --> 01:20:13,610
Ah!

1109
01:20:14,570 --> 01:20:15,650
Ah!

1110
01:20:18,930 --> 01:20:19,470
Ah!

1111
01:20:19,471 --> 01:20:20,471
Ah!

1112
01:20:21,870 --> 01:20:22,950
Ah!

1113
01:20:23,470 --> 01:20:24,010
Ah!

1114
01:20:24,011 --> 01:20:24,450
Ah!

1115
01:20:24,451 --> 01:20:24,710
Ah!

1116
01:20:24,711 --> 01:20:25,050
Ah!

1117
01:20:25,051 --> 01:20:25,170
Ah!

1118
01:20:25,410 --> 01:20:26,410
Ah!

1119
01:20:30,210 --> 01:20:31,470
I've had it!

1120
01:20:32,250 --> 01:20:34,170
Just a little bit further!

1121
01:20:34,670 --> 01:20:36,570
You piece of garbage!

1122
01:21:10,880 --> 01:21:12,930
His scent... he's moving away.

1123
01:21:15,090 --> 01:21:17,030
That was close.

1124
01:21:17,480 --> 01:21:18,480
What was?

1125
01:21:22,630 --> 01:21:26,390
But how did you... I
knew that it would work.

1126
01:21:27,270 --> 01:21:28,270
Hehehe.

1127
01:21:28,790 --> 01:21:29,830
My jacket!

1128
01:21:31,170 --> 01:21:35,850
You're so used to your own smell,
you didn't even notice it on the wind.

1129
01:21:36,670 --> 01:21:40,390
So you were skulking around in my jacket
to cover up your scent.

1130
01:21:41,050 --> 01:21:42,930
You seem to know a lot about tracking.

1131
01:21:43,250 --> 01:21:45,090
No wonder I couldn't smell you.

1132
01:21:45,650 --> 01:21:48,230
Guess I shouldn't be surprised,
right?

1133
01:21:49,990 --> 01:21:52,147
Seriously, how in the
world am I supposed to

1134
01:21:52,148 --> 01:21:54,410
keep track of somebody
who can split in half?

1135
01:21:54,990 --> 01:21:56,170
Well, come on then.

1136
01:22:04,070 --> 01:22:04,670
I don't know.

1137
01:22:04,671 --> 01:22:05,671
Please, wait.

1138
01:22:06,830 --> 01:22:09,930
From now on, we play for keeps.

1139
01:22:10,410 --> 01:22:14,550
My role now is to stall this person as
long as possible.

1140
01:22:14,770 --> 01:22:17,510
I would rather not resort to more powerful
attacks.

1141
01:22:17,850 --> 01:22:20,090
They will only leave me vulnerable to
defeat.

1142
01:22:20,370 --> 01:22:22,750
But my enemy is a formidable one.

1143
01:22:22,910 --> 01:22:26,090
I will have to reveal my secret technique
to best him.

1144
01:22:29,130 --> 01:22:30,190
Here I come!

1145
01:22:31,590 --> 01:22:34,410
I just had surgery, so I am not at my
best.

1146
01:22:34,610 --> 01:22:39,070
But if I only open the first gate,
the gate of opening, I should be alright.

1147
01:22:43,230 --> 01:22:45,330
The first gate, gate of opening!

1148
01:22:46,130 --> 01:22:47,130
Open!

1149
01:22:50,650 --> 01:22:51,690
Primary slowness!

1150
01:22:54,350 --> 01:22:57,190
The bone absorbed the impact of my kick!

1151
01:22:57,750 --> 01:22:59,670
Your speed is impressive.

1152
01:23:00,810 --> 01:23:02,370
But this is over now.

1153
01:23:03,430 --> 01:23:05,850
Dammit, I'm racking my brain here.

1154
01:23:05,990 --> 01:23:07,630
Why can't I come up with anything?

1155
01:23:09,510 --> 01:23:11,030
I'm at the end of my rope.

1156
01:23:11,110 --> 01:23:12,690
I can't hold on any longer.

1157
01:23:15,470 --> 01:23:17,610
You're staring death in the face.

1158
01:23:17,630 --> 01:23:20,130
Shouldn't you be screaming for mercy or
something?

1159
01:23:24,750 --> 01:23:26,090
Now die!

1160
01:23:27,190 --> 01:23:28,450
You're mine!

1161
01:23:29,110 --> 01:23:30,730
You're gonna die, kid!

1162
01:23:30,870 --> 01:23:32,450
Wipe that grin off your face!

1163
01:23:35,790 --> 01:23:37,770
What the hell?

1164
01:23:48,550 --> 01:23:50,470
Who are you?

1165
01:23:51,690 --> 01:23:53,370
Allies of the Leaf Village.

1166
01:23:54,270 --> 01:23:55,830
Where's Shinobi?

1167
01:23:56,550 --> 01:23:57,590
The sand.

1168
01:24:07,940 --> 01:24:08,940
Sand Ninja?

1169
01:24:08,970 --> 01:24:10,870
Am I still drunk or something?

1170
01:24:24,240 --> 01:24:25,500
Digital shrapnel!

1171
01:24:25,501 --> 01:24:26,501
No!

1172
01:24:28,620 --> 01:24:29,620
He

1173
01:24:40,500 --> 01:24:42,720
fired the bones from his fingertips?

1174
01:24:46,060 --> 01:24:47,280
Impulsive, aren't you?

1175
01:24:50,580 --> 01:24:51,780
You're different.

1176
01:24:53,500 --> 01:24:58,300
When you fought against me, you had much
more agility and sharpness.

1177
01:25:00,340 --> 01:25:02,360
I figured you would say that.

1178
01:25:03,100 --> 01:25:07,000
I am not the kind of person who holds a
grudge, even so.

1179
01:25:08,480 --> 01:25:11,440
Because of you, I've had a fairly tough
time of it.

1180
01:25:14,280 --> 01:25:15,280
Really?

1181
01:25:16,980 --> 01:25:19,100
Anyway, why have you come here?

1182
01:25:21,260 --> 01:25:22,980
I owe the Leaf...

1183
01:25:25,320 --> 01:25:27,620
I owe the Leaf a great debt.

1184
01:25:30,220 --> 01:25:31,220
Sasuke!

1185
01:25:32,200 --> 01:25:33,200
Sasuke!

1186
01:25:35,980 --> 01:25:36,980
Sasuke!

1187
01:25:37,720 --> 01:25:41,400
추천의 차례 I had heard something about how our
Village had finally made up with you

1188
01:25:41,401 --> 01:25:44,960
traitors, but I didn't expect you to
change sides so quickly.

1189
01:25:46,020 --> 01:25:49,080
It's not like we just attacked the Leaf
Village for kicks, you know.

1190
01:25:49,975 --> 01:25:51,120
We were following orders.

1191
01:25:52,720 --> 01:25:53,720
That's all.

1192
01:25:53,880 --> 01:25:55,500
Just like we're doing on this mission.

1193
01:25:56,600 --> 01:25:57,600
Hmm.

1194
01:25:58,240 --> 01:25:58,920
I get it.

1195
01:25:58,960 --> 01:26:00,640
The fifth Hokage sent them.

1196
01:26:01,390 --> 01:26:02,420
She saved our butts.

1197
01:26:03,900 --> 01:26:08,000
By the way, you seem a lot dumber than the
last time our paths crossed.

1198
01:26:08,400 --> 01:26:09,400
Huh?

1199
01:26:10,240 --> 01:26:11,240
Hmm.

1200
01:26:11,860 --> 01:26:13,580
So are you gonna give up again this time?

1201
01:26:14,760 --> 01:26:16,700
Go ahead, I'll take care of this for you.

1202
01:26:17,320 --> 01:26:20,240
Well, I'm sorry to disappoint you,
but I'm not about to give up.

1203
01:26:20,475 --> 01:26:23,780
And besides, a real man doesn't let a
woman do his fighting for him.

1204
01:26:23,781 --> 01:26:24,400
Hmm.

1205
01:26:24,401 --> 01:26:25,401
Huh.

1206
01:26:25,550 --> 01:26:27,860
Still being all macho with the man and
woman stuff?

1207
01:26:28,570 --> 01:26:30,640
You talk tough, but I know it's just an
act.

1208
01:26:30,940 --> 01:26:31,940
Idiot.

1209
01:26:35,120 --> 01:26:37,340
So this time you're on the Leaf side,
huh?

1210
01:26:37,560 --> 01:26:40,020
You guys are all over the place,
aren't ya?

1211
01:26:40,925 --> 01:26:43,540
The sound of the flute summons her
genjutsu.

1212
01:26:43,660 --> 01:26:44,660
I got it.

1213
01:26:45,380 --> 01:26:46,820
Cyclone Sight Jutsu!

1214
01:26:57,480 --> 01:26:59,191
She's deflecting the
sound of the flute and

1215
01:26:59,192 --> 01:27:02,121
nailing our opponent
with a physical attack.

1216
01:27:02,500 --> 01:27:05,160
She can attack and defend at the same
time.

1217
01:27:05,340 --> 01:27:07,300
That's a pretty handy jutsu to have.

1218
01:27:14,600 --> 01:27:16,940
It's like that girl was born to fight me!

1219
01:27:21,385 --> 01:27:23,460
Well, I don't see him.

1220
01:27:23,780 --> 01:27:26,500
I guess Ukon must have taken him out
already.

1221
01:27:34,280 --> 01:27:36,440
So you fight with puppets?

1222
01:27:38,840 --> 01:27:39,880
Behind you!

1223
01:27:43,440 --> 01:27:44,480
It's no use!

1224
01:27:44,740 --> 01:27:45,740
I can't move!

1225
01:27:46,360 --> 01:27:47,860
What is this guy?

1226
01:27:50,500 --> 01:27:52,320
He's all yours, Sakon!

1227
01:27:52,520 --> 01:27:53,520
Finish him!

1228
01:27:55,980 --> 01:27:57,100
I'll get you!

1229
01:27:57,101 --> 01:27:57,560
Be careful!

1230
01:27:58,100 --> 01:28:01,020
He's about to try and enter your body and
combine with it!

1231
01:28:01,580 --> 01:28:02,800
It's too late!

1232
01:28:21,540 --> 01:28:26,900
I guess that jutsu of yours doesn't really
work on puppets, does it?

1233
01:28:27,980 --> 01:28:29,520
This one's a puppet too!

1234
01:28:33,700 --> 01:28:39,060
Fair warning, we Sand Ninja aren't
pushovers, like our friends from the Leaf.

1235
01:28:39,600 --> 01:28:43,500
Oh, and standing as close as you are to my
friend the Black Ant?

1236
01:28:46,540 --> 01:28:47,680
Big mistake.

1237
01:28:52,920 --> 01:28:55,725
I hated going up
against the Sand Ninja as

1238
01:28:55,726 --> 01:28:59,581
enemies, but as allies,
they're pretty amazing.

1239
01:29:15,800 --> 01:29:16,880
That hurt.

1240
01:29:17,120 --> 01:29:18,200
You take over, brother.

1241
01:29:18,300 --> 01:29:20,300
Let me rest at this body a little bit
first.

1242
01:29:20,620 --> 01:29:22,420
You're so pathetic, Sakon.

1243
01:29:22,980 --> 01:29:24,780
Just who are these freaks?

1244
01:29:24,960 --> 01:29:26,940
This is their most dangerous ability.

1245
01:29:28,500 --> 01:29:31,820
I can't believe you let that puppet get
you off guard.

1246
01:29:32,540 --> 01:29:34,540
Well, you can be sure I won't.

1247
01:29:35,500 --> 01:29:38,860
Its puny power and speed are nothing
special.

1248
01:29:39,280 --> 01:29:41,720
It'll take more than this toy to stop me.

1249
01:29:43,680 --> 01:29:45,920
His wounds are already back to normal.

1250
01:29:46,240 --> 01:29:48,280
That healing ability is unbelievable.

1251
01:29:51,679 --> 01:29:55,280
I'm not usually the one who turns into the
main body.

1252
01:29:55,580 --> 01:29:57,540
It's hard to move like this.

1253
01:29:58,060 --> 01:30:00,820
This isn't the kind of enemy you can beat
head to head.

1254
01:30:00,821 --> 01:30:02,700
Back down and we'll regroup.

1255
01:30:04,560 --> 01:30:08,040
I can't back down when they show me no
respect.

1256
01:30:24,530 --> 01:30:28,270
My Black Ant puppet isn't designed to be
used on offense.

1257
01:30:28,630 --> 01:30:31,070
Its usual function is trapping people.

1258
01:30:31,071 --> 01:30:37,251
But when the Black Ant is paired with the
Crow, it makes a deadly attack combination.

1259
01:30:37,370 --> 01:30:38,810
Hey, you punks!

1260
01:30:38,811 --> 01:30:40,130
Let me out of here!

1261
01:30:40,470 --> 01:30:41,810
Can you hear me?

1262
01:30:55,890 --> 01:30:57,610
Secret Black move!

1263
01:30:57,950 --> 01:30:59,050
Iron Maiden!

1264
01:31:01,070 --> 01:31:02,070
I'm going to kill you!

1265
01:31:13,150 --> 01:31:14,740
She must be hiding around here.

1266
01:31:15,430 --> 01:31:18,200
I told you to explain the situation to me,
that's all.

1267
01:31:18,970 --> 01:31:24,520
You have no idea what kind of powers I
have.

1268
01:31:25,105 --> 01:31:28,365
If she thinks she can hide
from me, but stay close

1269
01:31:28,366 --> 01:31:31,600
enough so the sound of
her flute can still reach me...

1270
01:31:33,300 --> 01:31:34,760
She's mistaken.

1271
01:31:35,470 --> 01:31:36,720
All right!

1272
01:31:38,280 --> 01:31:40,040
Summoning Blade Dance!

1273
01:31:41,860 --> 01:31:42,860
Slash!

1274
01:31:45,000 --> 01:31:46,280
All right.

1275
01:31:46,480 --> 01:31:48,180
I'm far enough away.

1276
01:31:48,340 --> 01:31:49,820
It's time for my Genjutsu.

1277
01:31:51,230 --> 01:31:52,230
Huh?

1278
01:31:54,280 --> 01:31:55,260
Ah!

1279
01:31:55,261 --> 01:31:56,261
Ah!

1280
01:31:56,520 --> 01:31:57,520
Ah!

1281
01:32:02,340 --> 01:32:03,340
Ah!

1282
01:32:03,440 --> 01:32:04,380
Ah!

1283
01:32:04,381 --> 01:32:12,381
I'm going to kill you!

1284
01:32:21,870 --> 01:32:22,870
How was that?

1285
01:32:24,030 --> 01:32:25,030
It's finished.

1286
01:32:25,950 --> 01:32:26,950
Huh?

1287
01:32:27,350 --> 01:32:29,110
She doesn't mess around, huh?

1288
01:32:29,530 --> 01:32:31,130
She's as subtle as a rhino.

1289
01:32:31,290 --> 01:32:33,510
She might even be scarier than my mom.

1290
01:32:35,390 --> 01:32:36,390
Pretty good, huh?

1291
01:32:38,290 --> 01:32:39,290
Oh well.

1292
01:32:39,910 --> 01:32:40,470
Heh.

1293
01:32:40,810 --> 01:32:43,670
This time I guess I should be grateful
she's so scary.

1294
01:32:47,650 --> 01:32:55,650
I'll handle this.

1295
01:33:08,310 --> 01:33:08,930
No, please!

1296
01:33:09,310 --> 01:33:10,310
Just back me up!

1297
01:33:15,190 --> 01:33:17,590
I've got sand in my mouth!

1298
01:33:18,765 --> 01:33:20,550
Will you please let go of me?

1299
01:33:25,970 --> 01:33:28,850
You're not doing anything in your present
state.

1300
01:33:29,950 --> 01:33:31,150
I've got this.

1301
01:33:31,151 --> 01:33:33,450
You're Gaara of the Desert.

1302
01:33:35,780 --> 01:33:37,030
You wield sand.

1303
01:33:37,370 --> 01:33:38,670
Hence the name.

1304
01:33:48,980 --> 01:33:51,400
That sand is a strong defense.

1305
01:33:52,960 --> 01:33:56,360
But he's definitely not the close combat
type.

1306
01:33:57,580 --> 01:34:00,680
Getting close will probably be difficult,
though.

1307
01:34:01,620 --> 01:34:02,620
I'm going to kill you!

1308
01:34:06,000 --> 01:34:06,820
I'm going to kill you!

1309
01:34:06,821 --> 01:34:06,840
I'm going to kill you!

1310
01:34:06,960 --> 01:34:07,960
Hmm.

1311
01:34:09,020 --> 01:34:10,320
DJ, don't fret now!

1312
01:34:16,600 --> 01:34:19,060
His attacks and defense are as one.

1313
01:34:19,660 --> 01:34:21,660
All achieved with sand.

1314
01:34:22,960 --> 01:34:25,564
But the sand which
he can wield is probably

1315
01:34:25,565 --> 01:34:28,521
limited to the amount
that fits in that gourd.

1316
01:34:30,240 --> 01:34:33,080
Why else would you go through the trouble
of lugging it around?

1317
01:34:39,810 --> 01:34:41,010
Sand shower.

1318
01:34:42,790 --> 01:34:43,990
What a surprise.

1319
01:34:44,570 --> 01:34:51,690
If I need more sand, I can easily use the
earth we're standing on to make more.

1320
01:34:52,090 --> 01:34:52,910
Of course.

1321
01:34:53,110 --> 01:34:54,190
Now I see.

1322
01:34:54,450 --> 01:34:58,290
All of this time he has been feeding his
own sand into the ground.

1323
01:34:58,490 --> 01:35:02,470
And using it to grind up the stones and
minerals in the earth beneath us.

1324
01:35:02,930 --> 01:35:04,390
Creating new sand.

1325
01:35:06,070 --> 01:35:07,530
Gaara of the Desert.

1326
01:35:07,531 --> 01:35:10,150
They do not call him that for nothing.

1327
01:35:10,830 --> 01:35:11,830
Maisie.

1328
01:35:16,550 --> 01:35:17,750
You did it!

1329
01:35:18,250 --> 01:35:19,250
Almost.

1330
01:35:20,950 --> 01:35:22,390
Sand burial!

1331
01:35:33,750 --> 01:35:34,750
Ah!

1332
01:35:40,970 --> 01:35:41,970
Impossible!

1333
01:35:49,130 --> 01:35:51,850
That sure was a lot of pressure.

1334
01:35:53,810 --> 01:35:57,233
If I hadn't grown a membrane
of bone underneath my

1335
01:35:57,234 --> 01:35:59,890
skin, I would have been
crushed beyond recognition.

1336
01:36:00,490 --> 01:36:01,490
More bones.

1337
01:36:01,570 --> 01:36:02,670
He's a monster.

1338
01:36:02,930 --> 01:36:03,930
A freak.

1339
01:36:04,150 --> 01:36:05,990
Well, he certainly is a nuisance.

1340
01:36:07,530 --> 01:36:09,290
I underestimated you.

1341
01:36:10,210 --> 01:36:13,210
But that's the last time I'll get caught
in your sand.

1342
01:36:16,770 --> 01:36:18,330
Sand tsunami!

1343
01:36:31,650 --> 01:36:39,650
You will pay for this!

1344
01:36:39,651 --> 01:36:41,051
But of course, you'll pay for this!

1345
01:36:48,520 --> 01:36:51,640
To think that he could change the terrain
itself!

1346
01:37:11,700 --> 01:37:16,910
He is so powerful!

1347
01:37:16,911 --> 01:37:20,030
He is even stronger than when we fought
each other!

1348
01:37:22,580 --> 01:37:25,490
Well, surely this time...

1349
01:37:26,520 --> 01:37:27,910
Why won't he give up?

1350
01:37:28,130 --> 01:37:29,130
What?

1351
01:37:33,850 --> 01:37:34,950
I'm still alive.

1352
01:37:36,210 --> 01:37:39,510
If so, there must be a reason for it.

1353
01:37:42,990 --> 01:37:47,370
We descend upon the village hidden in the
mist under the cover of night.

1354
01:37:47,610 --> 01:37:49,890
We all feel the sting of the reaper.

1355
01:37:49,910 --> 01:37:50,910
And the recent betrayal.

1356
01:37:51,090 --> 01:37:54,530
Well, tonight they'll see savagery like
they've never known!

1357
01:37:59,190 --> 01:38:04,830
Show these scum the ferocity of our clan
down to every last man, woman and child!

1358
01:38:06,750 --> 01:38:09,410
What are you waiting for, Kimimaro?

1359
01:38:09,670 --> 01:38:11,010
Get going already!

1360
01:38:11,970 --> 01:38:13,590
I'm not sure what to do.

1361
01:38:14,410 --> 01:38:15,890
What's there to think about?

1362
01:38:16,210 --> 01:38:20,671
Go down to the village of the mist and kill
every single person... you come across!

1363
01:38:23,550 --> 01:38:25,790
Just follow your instincts.

1364
01:38:26,310 --> 01:38:27,850
It'll come to you.

1365
01:38:34,730 --> 01:38:37,230
Are you from the mist village?

1366
01:38:43,130 --> 01:38:44,130
No.

1367
01:38:46,990 --> 01:38:48,390
I... I see.

1368
01:38:48,590 --> 01:38:49,590
Sorry.

1369
01:38:56,030 --> 01:38:56,590
This is the closes door.

1370
01:38:56,591 --> 01:38:58,230
Haku... I'll go get some
drinks on before now.

1371
01:38:58,231 --> 01:38:58,790
No, it's nothing.

1372
01:38:59,010 --> 01:39:00,651
I feel a bit like...
Sorry, Zabuza.

1373
01:39:00,870 --> 01:39:03,030
We don't have time for daydreaming.

1374
01:39:03,230 --> 01:39:04,390
Better get on with your life.

1375
01:39:04,910 --> 01:39:05,910
Right.

1376
01:39:10,050 --> 01:39:11,450
His eyes were in the defect.

1377
01:39:12,290 --> 01:39:13,810
It was only so before I met Zabuza.

1378
01:39:23,590 --> 01:39:24,590
Ahh!

1379
01:39:30,095 --> 01:39:31,040
One moment!

1380
01:39:31,041 --> 01:39:32,041
Just a moment.

1381
01:39:53,440 --> 01:40:01,440
A little pause... and we are back.

1382
01:40:01,860 --> 01:40:03,940
What a bunch of idiots.

1383
01:40:04,440 --> 01:40:07,700
They understand nothing other than the
sword.

1384
01:40:09,420 --> 01:40:14,900
The days are gone when a horde of savages
could go slaughtering all in their path.

1385
01:40:15,980 --> 01:40:19,820
Brute strength is nothing in the face of a
regimented military.

1386
01:40:20,920 --> 01:40:23,280
These fools are rushing to their death.

1387
01:40:38,850 --> 01:40:39,850
I'm alone.

1388
01:40:40,710 --> 01:40:41,710
Again.

1389
01:40:54,855 --> 01:40:55,890
Why are you here?

1390
01:40:55,891 --> 01:40:57,571
Why are you blooming in a place like this?

1391
01:41:00,280 --> 01:41:01,810
How come you won't answer me, huh?

1392
01:41:05,370 --> 01:41:07,730
Oh, so you're going to ignore me too,
then.

1393
01:41:08,275 --> 01:41:09,710
Who cares anyway?

1394
01:41:10,070 --> 01:41:12,230
It's not like anyone will see you here!

1395
01:41:12,890 --> 01:41:13,930
That will do.

1396
01:41:17,250 --> 01:41:21,250
Maybe, just maybe, there is no purpose in
life.

1397
01:41:23,090 --> 01:41:29,610
But if you linger a while longer, you might
discover something of value in this world.

1398
01:41:29,905 --> 01:41:32,630
Like how you discovered that flower.

1399
01:41:33,610 --> 01:41:37,430
Or how I discovered you one fateful night.

1400
01:41:41,410 --> 01:41:43,710
Come, it's time to go.

1401
01:41:48,550 --> 01:41:54,950
I was put on this Earth to protect Lord
Orochimaru and his ambitions.

1402
01:41:55,110 --> 01:41:57,830
I was put on this Earth to protect Lord
Orochimaru and his ambitions.

1403
01:41:59,510 --> 01:42:01,570
I must welcome them, Atellans.

1404
01:42:01,571 --> 01:42:09,571
I was祈。」 Ganon!

1405
01:42:48,331 --> 01:42:51,530
As the last자 Is that the best you can do
with your ultimate defense?

1406
01:42:51,990 --> 01:42:53,030
King Galgal Gear Al lean?

1407
01:42:53,031 --> 01:42:53,450
w measures.

1408
01:42:53,451 --> 01:42:54,810
I'm a libraries of death.

1409
01:42:55,550 --> 01:42:56,550
Alexander Algo.

1410
01:43:00,330 --> 01:43:01,470
I see.

1411
01:43:01,790 --> 01:43:03,890
An armor-like shell of sand.

1412
01:43:04,250 --> 01:43:06,290
He is not your only opponent!

1413
01:43:21,850 --> 01:43:23,990
That might have been the end.

1414
01:43:23,991 --> 01:43:27,470
If Gaara had not intervened...

1415
01:43:28,390 --> 01:43:30,670
My body is still too weak.

1416
01:43:32,565 --> 01:43:34,750
I am only a burden to him like this.

1417
01:43:38,370 --> 01:43:40,290
I'm tired of that sand.

1418
01:43:41,590 --> 01:43:42,890
Very well, Gaara.

1419
01:43:43,050 --> 01:43:44,130
You first.

1420
01:43:54,890 --> 01:43:56,030
His spine!

1421
01:43:56,370 --> 01:43:57,570
How is it possible?

1422
01:44:01,230 --> 01:44:02,410
Clematis Dance!

1423
01:44:03,550 --> 01:44:05,610
First, the vine.

1424
01:44:09,270 --> 01:44:17,170
Then, the flower.

1425
01:44:22,730 --> 01:44:24,730
This bone is my strongest.

1426
01:44:26,670 --> 01:44:30,270
It will bore right through you,
defenses and all.

1427
01:44:31,450 --> 01:44:33,570
I don't have much time.

1428
01:44:36,510 --> 01:44:38,690
My ultimate defense!

1429
01:44:39,130 --> 01:44:40,590
Shukaku's shield!

1430
01:44:57,930 --> 01:44:59,090
It's so strong.

1431
01:44:59,091 --> 01:45:02,870
I took the hardest minerals in the soil I
gathered.

1432
01:45:03,070 --> 01:45:06,630
And then I fused them with the sand using
my chakra.

1433
01:45:10,050 --> 01:45:11,050
Tell me.

1434
01:45:11,570 --> 01:45:13,930
That's a very unusual jutsu.

1435
01:45:14,390 --> 01:45:16,510
It's a kekkei genkai, right?

1436
01:45:17,230 --> 01:45:19,150
It belonged to the Kaguya.

1437
01:45:19,750 --> 01:45:23,270
But now, it belongs to me and me alone.

1438
01:45:24,010 --> 01:45:26,510
You're the last of your clan, eh?

1439
01:45:26,511 --> 01:45:29,910
Then your clan perishes today.

1440
01:45:31,050 --> 01:45:33,670
That might very well be the case.

1441
01:45:34,070 --> 01:45:35,990
My body has weakened.

1442
01:45:36,310 --> 01:45:38,470
It may not last much longer.

1443
01:45:39,890 --> 01:45:40,890
However...

1444
01:45:41,530 --> 01:45:43,630
I will still live on.

1445
01:45:46,790 --> 01:45:49,390
Because... I am not alone.

1446
01:45:52,930 --> 01:45:54,990
You're not alone, you say?

1447
01:45:55,290 --> 01:45:56,250
That's right.

1448
01:45:56,251 --> 01:46:01,290
My existence has been subsumed into Lord
Orochimaru's ambition.

1449
01:46:03,770 --> 01:46:09,050
That means a part of me will survive in
Lord Orochimaru's heart forever.

1450
01:46:11,450 --> 01:46:13,430
Orochimaru's brainwashed you well.

1451
01:46:14,170 --> 01:46:16,210
You sad little pawn.

1452
01:46:21,200 --> 01:46:22,200
I put

1453
01:46:25,940 --> 01:46:27,160
a lot into this battle.

1454
01:46:27,760 --> 01:46:28,900
Almost out of chakra.

1455
01:46:28,901 --> 01:46:31,680
I must make this last thing count.

1456
01:46:43,840 --> 01:46:48,020
I will bury you two hundred meters below
the surface of the earth.

1457
01:46:48,200 --> 01:46:51,600
Under pressure so great you won't be able
to move a finger.

1458
01:46:52,260 --> 01:46:54,460
Imprisoned there till the end of time.

1459
01:47:12,160 --> 01:47:13,160
I will destroy you.

1460
01:47:14,800 --> 01:47:15,800
Bracken dance.

1461
01:47:34,680 --> 01:47:35,680
Thank you, Gaara.

1462
01:47:36,115 --> 01:47:37,730
You saved me again.

1463
01:47:38,405 --> 01:47:40,310
These powers of yours are truly
remarkable.

1464
01:47:40,770 --> 01:47:41,530
Not really.

1465
01:47:41,630 --> 01:47:44,130
I'm merely able to make the sand do my
bidding.

1466
01:47:44,730 --> 01:47:46,390
It's second nature to me now.

1467
01:47:48,460 --> 01:47:51,150
A tenacious opponent, but this time it's
over.

1468
01:47:52,680 --> 01:47:55,070
We won't be seeing him again in this life.

1469
01:47:55,250 --> 01:47:56,250
Yes, good.

1470
01:47:59,230 --> 01:48:01,010
My strength is gone.

1471
01:48:01,970 --> 01:48:02,970
We must descend.

1472
01:48:04,240 --> 01:48:05,690
I am not his pawn.

1473
01:48:07,090 --> 01:48:08,670
He is the one.

1474
01:48:09,010 --> 01:48:12,090
The only one who ever gave my life
meaning.

1475
01:48:13,410 --> 01:48:17,150
But how could the likes of you ever
understand that?

1476
01:48:30,400 --> 01:48:31,740
He is dead.

1477
01:48:35,300 --> 01:48:36,380
Can it be?

1478
01:48:37,360 --> 01:48:38,360
Kimimaro?

1479
01:48:39,400 --> 01:48:40,400
No matter.

1480
01:48:41,140 --> 01:48:42,800
He's of no further use to me.

1481
01:48:44,245 --> 01:48:47,860
All that matters now is that Sasuke is
coming.

1482
01:48:49,280 --> 01:48:51,420
And of his own free will.

1483
01:48:51,920 --> 01:48:54,420
Just as I foretold.

1484
01:48:54,900 --> 01:48:55,900
Sasuke.

1485
01:48:57,740 --> 01:48:58,460
Sasuke.

1486
01:48:58,660 --> 01:48:59,660
What a sheer luck.

1487
01:49:00,340 --> 01:49:01,480
I should have been killed.

1488
01:49:01,940 --> 01:49:03,640
No, it was not meant to be.

1489
01:49:04,570 --> 01:49:06,360
My sensei has often said to me.

1490
01:49:07,140 --> 01:49:09,340
A good ninja always makes his own luck.

1491
01:49:10,050 --> 01:49:11,780
That meddlesome mother hen.

1492
01:49:12,340 --> 01:49:14,000
Gai-sensei is nothing of the sort.

1493
01:49:14,440 --> 01:49:17,120
I am very grateful to you for having saved
my life.

1494
01:49:17,600 --> 01:49:18,340
But I warn you.

1495
01:49:18,380 --> 01:49:21,360
I will not abide anyone speaking ill of my
sensei.

1496
01:49:23,340 --> 01:49:24,860
So you're another one, eh?

1497
01:49:25,740 --> 01:49:26,260
Hm?

1498
01:49:26,261 --> 01:49:31,840
You have someone in your life whom you
honor and revere so much that every hurt

1499
01:49:31,841 --> 01:49:35,240
inflicted on them is inflicted on you as
well.

1500
01:49:35,520 --> 01:49:38,920
And the closer they are to you,
the greater the pain.

1501
01:49:39,880 --> 01:49:43,220
To feel so strongly for someone you would
fight for them.

1502
01:49:44,840 --> 01:49:46,260
And die for them.

1503
01:49:47,160 --> 01:49:50,160
You and Naruto Uzumaki have that in
common.

1504
01:49:50,500 --> 01:49:51,500
No.

1505
01:49:52,760 --> 01:49:53,320
However.

1506
01:49:53,640 --> 01:49:56,240
What if this person you honor and revere.

1507
01:49:56,241 --> 01:49:58,660
Would even die for as not a virtuous
person?

1508
01:49:59,020 --> 01:50:00,020
Impossible!

1509
01:50:00,200 --> 01:50:04,320
Such a person would be unworthy of honor
or respect.

1510
01:50:04,720 --> 01:50:04,960
No.

1511
01:50:05,520 --> 01:50:08,880
Perhaps the companionship of even an evil
person.

1512
01:50:09,280 --> 01:50:11,480
Is preferable to loneliness.

1513
01:50:21,260 --> 01:50:22,260
Sasuke!

1514
01:50:39,860 --> 01:50:41,680
I am in your hands!

1515
01:50:42,300 --> 01:50:42,860
No!

1516
01:50:42,861 --> 01:50:43,140
Kamehameha!

1517
01:50:43,141 --> 01:50:44,560
You are so beautiful.

1518
01:50:46,000 --> 01:50:47,000
I don't know everything.

1519
01:50:47,120 --> 01:50:48,120
No!

1520
01:50:48,320 --> 01:50:50,160
This is the only one!

1521
01:50:50,700 --> 01:50:51,260
No!

1522
01:50:51,600 --> 01:50:51,740
I want it!

1523
01:50:51,741 --> 01:50:52,060
That's my first time.

1524
01:50:52,260 --> 01:50:53,380
Shut up.

1525
01:50:54,380 --> 01:50:55,380
Stop it.

1526
01:51:16,840 --> 01:51:24,840
A little pause... and we are back.

1527
01:51:46,920 --> 01:51:54,920
A little pause... and we are back.

1528
01:51:54,940 --> 01:51:56,300
A little pause... and we are back.

